    "body": "I'm not sure what \"semantics of the element\" means, do you mean the behavior of the `label` attribute?\nSo that we can't change what label do based on `appearance`.\n\n---\n\nAnyway, there is another workaround than avoid duplication of the select/options, but is also more risky:\n```css\nselect, select::picker(select) {\n  appearance: base-select;\n}\n\n@supports (appearance: base-select) {\nselect [data-text]::before {\n    content: attr(data-text) / attr(data-text);\n  }\n}\n\n@supports not (appearance: base-select) {\n  select option [hidden] {\n    display: initial;\n  }\n\n  select legend {\n    display: none;\n  }\n}\n```\n```html\n...\n<optgroup label=\"plain text\">\n\n    <legend>\n      <span hidden>plain text</span>\n      <span data-text=\"rich content text\"></span> \n    </legend>\n\n    <option>\n      <span hidden>plain text</span>\n      <span data-text=\"rich content text\"></span>\n    </option>\n\n  </optgroup>\n...\n```\n(Assuming the author doesn't need wrapper elements around `<option>`. Otherwise, duplication is currently necessary to support Firefox across all platforms.)\nhttps://codepen.io/sb3nder/pen/GgWWOGW?editors=1100",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
